#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115062 :question/id #uuid "87bf279f-9f78-54cb-b9c3-e1bf1c5426ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-4505" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x &=5 \\\\ -5x+6y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y &=5 \\\\ -5x+6y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\nA = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}2 & 0 \\\\ - 5 & 6\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}2 & 0 \\\\ - 5 & 6\\end{array} \\right]}\n\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115063 :question/id #uuid "359f4b72-60d2-54e2-b7ef-c48f1e3af708" :question/math-academy-id "e-4506" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5y &=-3x \\\\ 6+x &=-2+y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y &=0 \\\\ x-y &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\nA = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 5 \\\\ 1 & - 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 5 \\\\ 1 & - 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115064 :question/id #uuid "b87aa5eb-f689-5f34-baeb-f97c3f200552" :question/math-academy-id "e-4507" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}10 & - 15 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 \\\\ - 2\\end{array} \\right]}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-15y &=5 \\\\ 1x+0y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y &=1 \\\\ x &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac702230-e0b6-5149-946f-efd4c6240c5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111962} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d139bd-6d1e-5f66-a303-7e6b7a0e51de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111963} {:answer/id #uuid "d2848f95-94e5-5ab3-a0