trices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-5$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $9$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $9$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y &=9 \\\\ 0x-5y &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299618 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4594da98-1c2a-54d9-8a10-751dc6d6a248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297837}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297837} :answer-field/id #uuid "10cf71a3-1902-5e22-a831-1fd47e406b59" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c8b4bec-ca96-58d1-b394-40b30e168da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298237}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298237} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5be443-392a-5f65-a6a9-f11df9b70cc9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe58c66-d1d9-590f-a96b-927875901a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297623}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297623} :answer-field/id #uuid "b89b4d3f-1939-5756-b8ce-99a1e27fc048" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e2b4b0-4685-5ae3-bafc-e5d93e75a043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298584}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298584} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce53df6e-e873-51c6-b370-bb132a5e6f60" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ee62c6ba-71ac-57ec-bfe8-410ce9e1a842" :question/math-academy-id "q-317536" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4y-x &=3 \\\\ 9y+2x &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $5$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4y &=3 \\\\ 2x+9y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299619 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbb4dbdb-c501-59e8-a1dd-8b0bd23d0eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298495}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298495} :answer-field/id #uuid "1389ccbd-1b7a-5cb1-88d4-2ed1133983fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de79627-eef5-5970-8e2d-eb52b1f0edc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297875}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297875} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b31d414-76e7-5210-916c-0c91bb636d73" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298788} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee7737ea-f780-5480-b74d-28a0673efadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298564}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298564} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ca17d4e-624f-5422-818c-6a97ee47e9d7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299152} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb8f547b-4751-5ed3-a16b-868f68570f62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298624}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298624} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5360a1e-9e7d-5e50-a64b-89bdb7d29784" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "042fab86-9bc5-5bac-af22-a67d3b6956f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-317540" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4 &=x \\\\ -7 &=3+y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | $1$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-10$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-10$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y &=4 \\\\ 0x+y &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299621 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afa59dcb-f7ce-5c09-a4c8-22b3dd6c17f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298317} :answer-field/id #uuid "558975f8-6e41-52d2-a81c-63a261f8cee1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec1d54c2-8080-5c78-b74c-cea3bc22fc7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298556}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298556} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd39ba45-0c63-53b1-89a4-29f995bbc06a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d9d91921-5228-5fa0-a7a6-2fcbc61ddda4" :question/math-academy-id "q-317563" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $\\,4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,3.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix encodes the coefficients of $x$ and $y$, and the $2\\times 1$ vector on the right gives the constants, so the system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8x-4y &=16 \\\\ -6x+12y &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDividing the first equation by $4$ and the second by $-6$ gives the simplified system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=4 \\\\ x-2y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich matches the entries shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c13d0ca-65a8-51a3-a5d1-a0920f6683b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298017}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298017} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a629bbe-7d36-5b30-862e-39429be187c2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc7c405e-3476-5c14-a227-d3f55c63a900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298634}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298634} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d050fae-3c59-5211-82f2-626d6e3d2224" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "61031038-e22c-5885-b49a-a1823235ca68" :question/math-academy-id "q-317570" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y &=11 \\\\ -3x+2y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6aab5e-cd3c-5e96-95c4-087bae5528eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297865}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297865} :answer-field/id #uuid "477735a7-4ce2-51d0-ac73-6c78382c8e52" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8e6f31-d8cc-59a5-a7c1-8733b1f94e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298374}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298374} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ccb8e1-1b38-53eb-8622-5c815d1d251a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b07676ec-4252-579f-89b9-78b9cf7c6870" :question/math-academy-id "q-317582" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+1y &=5 \\\\ -1x+0y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=5 \\\\ -x &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82829b2e-baf5-5fab-a903-a5316f8d9f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298116} :answer-field/id #uuid "23562a54-29b9-5cdd-98d6-f06cb96d7dd5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298753} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44d0b073-d74e-5949-bc02-d145609dc06c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297834}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297834} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2e2fcd2-15bf-58c4-b88d-698133875b26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "267f94e4-48b2-5a54-9c3b-23086cc4a9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-317583" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+0y &=10 \\\\ -3x+2y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x &=10 \\\\ -3x+2y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13874c69-ce11-5c4a-b0db-84ef83ade9dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336218} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1b6947-b6e0-5826-8441-dbb3d0b931fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336883} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c180a6-138d-5a7f-9d31-a404b45cc073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337510} {:answer/id #uuid "ece790d0-e97b-5afe-a665-0bd073ac46d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338100} {:answer/id #uuid "fa94f849-7016-5d56-965c-7206ff571a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338230} :answer-field/id #uuid "19deb739-c9c7-5b2d-8ffb-a8a00f607b7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f3afffa-5f2d-5a4d-8c50-83d3e9705709" :question/math-academy-id "q-71800" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=7 \\\\ x+y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=7 \\\\ x+y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "092149d4-4746-597d-b469-fd9e124145a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336110} {:answer/id #uuid "0a6aba9a-03cf-5963-9982-db4dd212466f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336129} {:answer/id #uuid "734fe104-fc87-5937-ab79-b8a96359e482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337072} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c39530-814f-58b1-87ba-a2ce667a5978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337859} {:answer/id #uuid "ff0d859f-843c-5762-8a71-9acb0d107736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338271}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336110} :answer-field/id #uuid "77ca8a8e-7cde-5776-a055-3d15385c87dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6fb63d0f-068a-51bd-a44a-a1afcc574af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-71804" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y &=-1 \\\\ 5x &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. \nThe variable $y$ does not appear in the second equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y &=-1 \\\\ 5x+0y &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54be5f09-3b58-5930-bdc7-ccdb2f67d6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352318} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca99045-dd33-5f43-a7c8-c5f10727365c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352525} {:answer/id #uuid "8711bd28-d757-5733-8d8e-74aa8e1eeb4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352748} {:answer/id #uuid "87cd6a64-8926-5898-b3a1-08617a82941b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352758} {:answer/id #uuid "dfede72a-5a0f-52ab-9653-3586280ead39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352748} :answer-field/id #uuid "27886f52-60bd-58ac-8062-d0a079292caa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "302f133a-6090-5037-99fd-6973d6637f17" :question/math-academy-id "q-8820" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y &=1 \\\\ x-8y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y &=1 \\\\ x-8y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b3cd2b-284b-5242-a0fd-852bf0b1881c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5y &=-9 \\\\ x &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422744} {:answer/id #uuid "2540c038-f7ff-526e-8623-0b2eb9995f47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5y &=9 \\\\ x &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422762} {:answer/id #uuid "86106155-653b-5126-ac12-f97cdb674767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y &=9 \\\\ x &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422839} {:answer/id #uuid "9560da06-25ad-5721-bc24-046715bc8034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5y &=9 \\\\ x &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422854} {:answer/id #uuid "be15d0f0-70f8-5910-afd6-1af63be69956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y &=9 \\\\ y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422854} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4d849c-e24c-5150-9286-220ece393a3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a1162f6f-3b06-5edc-926f-fe3ac4ca244f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130528" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+5y &=9 \\\\ x+0y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5y &=9 \\\\ x &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2b0257b-5aa5-5961-8c79-b270612973ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=0 \\\\ x-4y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403497} {:answer/id #uuid "efe4f88d-8258-5d39-be46-855c1e2c58e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=0 \\\\ -4x+y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403498} {:answer/id #uuid "7cea8dbe-3578-5886-bfe4-f51b25347ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=0 \\\\ x-4y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403499} {:answer/id #uuid "aba3c242-ef16-5d89-8d0a-32ce47931725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=5 \\\\ x-4y &=0\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403500} {:answer/id #uuid "777783df-e9bd-5dfd-9c9a-d3ccfc310aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=0 \\\\ x-3y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403501}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403497} :answer-field/id #uuid "796fd7cb-3aaa-51b5-a9d2-6f0f250be044" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7f74fa12-0053-502d-b17f-669ab25e05d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-71854" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x-y &=0 \\\\ -3x+12y &=-15.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=0 \\\\ x-4y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2a9ff2e-cd07-5184-a748-73ab5a2d6469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604446}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604446} :answer-field/id #uuid "0feb7ced-b4bf-5741-ad36-a2148dc30e2f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604477} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9de62a0e-39f7-5eda-bc85-d8efb3f38800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604384}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604384} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcafc6de-7bf3-5d44-bb3a-ffe721ef67ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "28030764-dfab-5186-ade3-6ad982a69767" :question/math-academy-id "q-317581" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr><td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">\n{\n    </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"10\" width=\"100\">{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"10\" width=\"10\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"10\" width=\"10\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"40px\">\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"10\" width=\"100\">{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"10\" width=\"10\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"10\" width=\"10\">$\\,\\,-2.$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y &=7 \\\\ 0x+y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y &=7 \\\\ y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90cc1755-3b32-50cc-b1e6-ef23a46d69c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604369}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604369} :answer-field/id #uuid "59edda13-aa56-59d2-a2c1-31e7089761e2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604508} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26eeddf7-93c2-53bd-ad97-82b1061c68f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604248}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604248} :answer-field/id #uuid "721b7e6e-1bb7-5f00-ada8-f1dbf1715717" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604512} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f335d289-160c-598f-bf7e-435d8e515f13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604460}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604460} :answer-field/id #uuid "d42950d8-eb61-57e8-b18b-da5b2e9b5b24" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604542} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3405b0c-f0a1-5c1c-80fa-4d87429cefcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604461}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604461} :answer-field/id #uuid "eebb4c5c-83ec-5325-b46e-124dfb9b5470" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4c8ad85b-6e42-5b46-a5f5-5b11787c440b" :question/math-academy-id "q-317533" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y &=6 \\\\ 5y-2x &=0,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td><td>\n</td><td>\n</td><td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>$=$</td>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y &=6 \\\\ -2x+5y &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604609 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56428ccd-1ce7-5816-a899-435e1ac9183e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y+x &=1 \\\\ -2x &=8\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604309} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf1edc9-bdf7-5457-8ec9-e8f592989ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=2 \\\\ -2y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604355} {:answer/id #uuid "b3463627-ba39-5be5-afde-676336a272da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+y &=2 \\\\ x-2y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604399} {:answer/id #uuid "b3582981-6b87-58a6-ace2-43635eee5ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+y &=2 \\\\ y &=6\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604400} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4b9ceb-2f0d-5953-9ce6-17f5fd3bc469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+y &=2 \\\\ -2y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604412}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604412} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8e8861d-3639-5a9c-b966-676d3d269727" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f9355a7-de6b-578e-99a5-c8853736c1f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-32017" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+y &=2 \\\\ 0x-2y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+y &=2 \\\\ -2y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38cb783a-6cf7-5f17-961c-0c2082059c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604272} {:answer/id #uuid "8b09f947-acde-58af-ab0a-7b461ae58809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604361} {:answer/id #uuid "afa108c1-cbc3-5791-a361-9e8f180aabcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604397} {:answer/id #uuid "f599bda4-8506-586d-980b-5b70ba2d97ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604464} {:answer/id #uuid "f88d0a48-b832-5468-bac1-9eb7d313e9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604468}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604397} :answer-field/id #uuid "26e644b6-2e14-5572-a9c4-d5bbf06fe85e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604484}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a6bce15c-7366-5bbf-8596-fb4c6459f4a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130512" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3 &=-y \\\\ 0 &=-1-2x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+y &=-3 \\\\ 2x+0y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604616 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5459f0c-1eb6-5dba-828b-ab6a6f4e5a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604432} :answer-field/id #uuid "47f7f112-87ba-552d-9bb8-3ac461686805" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604500} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68e83df2-aba5-55a1-8fc1-ef2c2a65026d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604324}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604324} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a882650-5a0d-5009-9b74-8d5dda92188f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbd6285b-9b3d-5b05-83b8-c709475213de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604439}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604439} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1e5ed5f-7786-5034-9ae9-c27a1bb0f473" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604527} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cac4d593-370a-5637-be73-4fba331c6e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604423} :answer-field/id #uuid "f723ac45-173c-5f24-b300-04ee475710c3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ce1947c5-ab86-5a81-ab9f-f80633f35f4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-317518" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6y &=18 \\\\ 5x &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td><td>\n</td><td>\n</td><td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>$=$</td>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-20$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $x$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ Similarly, the variable $y$ does not appear in the second equation, which means that its coefficient is $0$ too. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x-6y &=18 \\\\ 5x+0y &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d51918f-f7a2-530a-93ba-8aa1dbff97a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604236} {:answer/id #uuid "66eb2540-892b-5054-a627-b0e911168b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604319} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b027b7-0143-5279-816e-8d13997ff02f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604388} {:answer/id #uuid "ada4f760-4b62-5d97-a72e-4fe27db835db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604394} {:answer/id #uuid "e90aa008-f624-5e7b-88aa-5b451ad76ca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604450}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604450} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae7c45bc-6cd0-5ead-ad70-0fd0273ce816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f90a2076-00d9-5a6f-a56a-3ae14ad4c0fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-12290" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y &=4 \\\\ x-6y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y &=4 \\\\ x-6y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}]}
